Subject: [PATCH] zephyr-chipyard-sw: drop a stray command from install_conda.sh

Line 6 of scripts/install_conda.sh is the literal text `scripts/install_conda.sh#`
-- a copy-paste slip in the comment header (upstream commit 0d4c3622 "update install
documentation" lost the leading `#`). Bash reads it as a command, so the script exits
127 before it does anything.

Nothing had ever caught it because every user of this repo so far bootstrapped from an
already-installed workspace. The first genuine from-scratch run dies here:

    scripts/install_conda.sh: line 6: scripts/install_conda.sh#: No such file or directory

The script is SOURCED by scripts/00_bootstrap.sh, so the failure takes the bootstrap
with it.

Restore the line to the comment it was meant to be. Applied by scripts/00_bootstrap.sh.
NOT upstream.

diff --git a/scripts/install_conda.sh b/scripts/install_conda.sh
index 86ca2381cba..34a3799c7bf 100644
--- a/scripts/install_conda.sh
+++ b/scripts/install_conda.sh
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 # Install Miniforge3 (Linux/x86_64) into ./tools/miniforge3 non-interactively,
 # then configure solver and install clang (lib + python bindings) + dotmap.
 # Re-runnable and idempotent.
-scripts/install_conda.sh#
+#
 # NOTE: This script is meant to be SOURCED, not executed.
 # When sourced, we must be careful not to set options that affect the parent shell.
 
